.TH GIT-PULL-BRANCHES 1 "2026-10-08" "Git Helpers" "git-helpers Manual"
.SH NAME
git-pull-branches \- pull updates on every local branch
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B git pull-branches
[\fB-n\fR | \fB--dry-run\fR]
[\fB-v\fR | \fB--verbose\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBgit-pull-branches\fR iterates through the repository's local branches, checks
out each one in turn, and runs \fBgit pull\fR. It repeats until no branch updates
change the repository state. The command refuses to run when there are unstaged or
staged changes in the working tree.
.PP
When run with \fB-n\fR or \fB--dry-run\fR, it reports which branches would be
updated without checking out or pulling anything. When run with \fB-v\fR or
\fB--verbose\fR, it prints additional progress messages to standard error.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B git pull-branches
Update all local branches from their configured remotes.
.TP
.B git pull-branches --dry-run
Report which branches would be updated without changing branch state.
.TP
.B git pull-branches -v
Show progress while each branch is updated.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git (1),
.BR git-pull (1)
